@4.12 GUI-DIALOGS.INC.BL -- every dialog as a verb (2)
=A list built a step at a time, out of an array or out of a bank
.
.  LIST.BEGIN title$, rows
.      OUT: a list box declared, not yet drawn
.
.  LIST.ARRAY count
.      IN: GUI.LIST.ITEM$()
.      OUT: its rows come from the array
.
.  LIST.BANK bank, first, last
.      IN: a RAM bank in the GP.BSTR image layout
.      OUT: its rows come from the bank
.
.  LISTTO.RUN
.      OUT: the row, or 0 cancelled
.
.  LIST.ITEM n
.      OUT: row n as text
.
.  LIST.SORT bank, first, last
.      OUT: that bank's rows in order, in place
.
:GP.SUB LIST.BEGIN, " OPEN FILE ", 12
:GP.SUB LIST.BANK, MY.BANK%, 0, N - 1
:SEL = GP.FN(LISTTO.RUN)
:IF SEL > 0 THEN F$ = GP.FN(LIST.ITEM, SEL)
.
.A bank list never comes into low memory. The bank holds the GP.BSTR image
.layout -- a 16-bit count at $A000, an offset a row at $A002, then the
.records -- and GUI.LIST.FETCH reads one row at a time, as it is drawn. That
.is how FILEPICK (SEC 4.20) shows a directory of any length in a program with
.no room for it. LIST.SORT moves the two-byte offsets and not the records, so
.a pointer into one stays good afterwards; it reaches the bank through
.STASH.SELECT, which is what lets the whole module sit inside a GP.BANKED
.region.
.
.Example: GUI.EXP.BL.
.
=EXAMPLE PROGRAM
.
.  GUI.EXP.BL -- runnable, in the GPC-BASIC folder
.
